        <p>I'm <strong>Conor O'Shea</strong>, an AI &amp; CS student who cares about the whole pipeline — not just the model, but the data, the deployment and the security implications around it.</p>
        <p>My work spans <strong>computer vision</strong> (YOLO pose estimation feeding custom <strong>LSTM</strong> temporal models), <strong>privacy engineering</strong> (redaction pipelines for sensitive email corpora), and <strong>LLM security</strong> research on how large language models handle adversarially obfuscated content.</p>
        <p>I also teach — building and delivering hands-on ML workshops for Edinburgh's student-led AI society. My goal: become an <strong>ML / Applied AI Engineer</strong> working on systems that are both capable and trustworthy.</p>
